course: dictionary
lesson: 7048
title: Passover: a festival word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Passover is the name of a special time, so it starts with a capital letter. A name like this is called a proper noun. The sentences tell you what it means: «Passover, or Pesach, is a spring festival remembering the Exodus from Egypt.» The words «spring festival» are the clue. A festival is a special day or time of celebration, and this one happens in spring.
explain: Look for the words in brackets, commas and "or". They often explain a hard word. «Passover, or Pesach,» tells you that Pesach is another name for the same festival. You don't need to know Pesach to understand the first part of the sentence.
explain: The sentences also tell you what happens at Passover. «At the Seder, families eat matzah, a flat bread made without yeast.» Matzah is a food, and the clue is "flat bread". Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
fact: Passover is a Jewish spring festival that remembers how God freed the Israelites from slavery in Egypt.
fact: The Seder is a special meal that families share at Passover.
fact: Matzah is flat bread made without yeast.
fact: Christians link Passover to Easter, because the Last Supper happened at Passover time.
fact: Passover is a proper noun, so it always starts with a capital letter.
exercise: «Passover, or Pesach, is a spring festival remembering the Exodus from Egypt.» What season is Passover in? | Autumn | Winter | Summer | *Spring
exercise: What is the special meal that families share at Passover called? | Pentecost | Good Friday | Exodus | *Seder
exercise: Which word means flat bread made without yeast? | Seder | Exodus | Pentecost | *Matzah
test: In the Bible, what did the angel of death pass over? | *Houses marked with lamb's blood | Gold paint on the walls | Red flags on the doors | Water from the Nile
test: Why do Christians link Passover to Easter? | Because Passover is a winter festival | Because Passover always falls on a Sunday | Because Pentecost comes at Passover | *Because the Last Supper happened at Passover time
exam: Which word is a proper noun, a name that starts with a capital letter? | festival | *Passover | spring | matzah
